This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

Its subject is scripts/render-vocabulary-index.sh and the `# vocabulary:` markers in
scripts/validate-enforcement-map.sh, both of which are this repository's own programs.
install.sh ships neither, and it does not write docs/vocabulary-index.md, so on a consumer
this fixture would resolve no renderer, no marker corpus and no index. Its controlA arm runs
`--check` against the real repo root, which on a consumer tree is a root that has none of
the three.

A fixture whose subject is absent cannot fail, and a unit that cannot fail scores as a pass
in the consumer's own suite verdict.

It is also a MUTATION BATTERY: it builds thirteen throwaway repos per run and edits copies
of the renderer's own marker corpus and owner files.
